# Pairs with ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted in ReplicationReBootstrap. After a source restore, an entry s logged
# under the old lineage can still reach r during the drain. Realigning on the
# pre-capture alone misses it, and a later pass deletes a value s never deleted.
MODULE: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeletedRealignOnOpenCaptureOnly
TARGET: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: realignment considers only entries captured at open, so a stale source entry taken during the drain is later reconciled as a delete
PERTURBS: EndExport

--- FIND
          /\ aligned' = IF ex.scope /\ stable /\ ~(orphan /\ ex.precap.o = s) /\ ~LateOrphan
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an entry taken during the drain does not block realignment.
          /\ aligned' = IF ex.scope /\ stable /\ ~(orphan /\ ex.precap.o = s)
--- END
